Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Environmental Drivers and Spatial Attribution of Habitat Change
Version: 0.21.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Explains where environmental changes improve or reduce fitted
    habitat suitability. Paired current and future scenarios produce spatial
    driver-only effects, retained-driver comparisons and overall habitat
    change using frozen model weights. Range diagnostics and model disagreement
    accompany the comparisons. Random forest, MaxEnt and generalized additive
    model engines support variable selection, spatial cross-validation,
    ensemble prediction and projection.
    Scenario attribution is a predictive explanation; presence-background
    suitability is not an occurrence probability or an identified causal effect.
